// A BODILESS MEMBER'S SIGNATURE IS CHECKED TOO (#810).
//
// `Required`/`Hook` members carry no body, and until now the checker
// stopped at exactly that: every reader of a signature resolved its names
// only where the function is USED, so a hook nobody could call had no
// resolved name in it at all. The same undefined name in a BODIED
// member's signature is refused (`sema_decl.check_body` reads the return
// through the ordinary queries); only the bodiless half was silent.
//
// Four faces, one mechanism -- each is a position `check_signature`
// reaches through the ordinary queries: a plain return, a generic's
// return, a generic's bound, a plain parameter.
//
// `.count 6`: four undeclared names here, plus the two standing stage-5
// placeholders in `std/env/env.zen` (`Actor`, `Ref` on `Env.spawn`,
// issue #810) that every test standing on `Env` reaches. They are
// deliberate and tracked, not cascade; when whichever of the ledger's
// (a)/(b)/(c) lands the total drops and this test still passes.

Box = {
    area* = (self: @Self) NoSuchPlainType

    give* = (self: @Self, w: NoSuchParam) ()

    make* = <T: NoSuchBound>(self: @Self, v: T) T

    take* = <T>(self: @Self, v: T) NoSuchGeneric<T>
}

main = (env: Env) Res<i32, AllocError> {
    println("unreachable");
    Ok(0);
}
